1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,110
There's a magnet in your pocket right now.

2
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:03,990
When your phone buzzes,

3
00:00:03,990 --> 00:00:07,880
that's a tiny motor spinning... and inside it sits a tiny,

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:09,280
very strong magnet.

5
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:12,660
Now check the spec sheet of an electric scooter or car.

6
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:14,480
Look at the motor line,

7
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:17,730
and you'll often see two words... permanent magnet.

8
00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:20,260
Same family of magnet, just bigger.

9
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,320
No magnet, no motor.

10
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,600
No motor... no E.V.

11
00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:26,750
And in 2025,

12
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:29,920
that one magnet hit India's E.V. makers hard.

13
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,600
July, Pune.

14
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:37,400
Bajaj's electric Chetak factory was making barely half the scooters it made a year earlier.

15
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:38,340
The reason?

16
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:39,440
Not a strike.

17
00:00:39,610 --> 00:00:40,500
Not batteries.

18
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:44,460
That small magnet... and most of them come from China.

19
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:46,370
In July 2024,

20
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:48,760
about 20,000 Chetaks a month.

21
00:00:49,070 --> 00:00:52,330
In July 2025... less than 11,000.

22
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:53,830
And the crazy part?

23
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:58,460
The raw material for that magnet is lying in the sand on our own beaches

24
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:00,180
— in Andhra Pradesh, Kerala,

25
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:01,640
Tamil Nadu and Odisha.

26
00:01:01,890 --> 00:01:03,630
By our own government's count,

27
00:01:03,630 --> 00:01:07,280
India's sands hold about 7 million tonnes of rare earths.

28
00:01:07,630 --> 00:01:09,670
So why can't India make the magnet?

29
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:12,110
Stay with me, and you'll see three things.

30
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,700
The hard step nobody else wanted to do.

31
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,680
Then, about six minutes in,

32
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:20,040
the secret inside our sand that kept it locked away.

33
00:01:20,230 --> 00:01:22,550
And at the end, the date you should watch.

34
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:25,430
First, what is this magnet?

35
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:27,670
It's called a rare earth magnet.

36
00:01:27,930 --> 00:01:29,040
It's mostly iron.

37
00:01:29,430 --> 00:01:32,450
Add a little boron... and one special metal,

38
00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:33,740
called neodymium.

39
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:36,160
It's small, but it's very strong.

40
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:38,980
And in a motor, strength is everything.

41
00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:39,900
Here's why.

42
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:43,670
A stronger magnet gives you the same push from a smaller motor.

43
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,480
Smaller means lighter.

44
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:48,920
And lighter means you get more kilometres on one charge.

45
00:01:49,210 --> 00:01:49,810
Makes sense?

46
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:52,790
That's why the spec sheet says permanent magnet.

47
00:01:53,130 --> 00:01:57,320
Most electric scooters and cars on the road use these magnets in their motors.

48
00:01:57,580 --> 00:01:58,890
And it's not just vehicles.

49
00:01:59,230 --> 00:02:00,680
Remember the buzz in your phone?

50
00:02:00,970 --> 00:02:01,950
Same kind of magnet.

51
00:02:02,370 --> 00:02:04,740
You'll also find it in many wind turbines,

52
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:06,160
and in defence systems.

53
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:07,660
Now look at this number.

54
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:11,510
India needs about 4,000 tonnes of these magnets a

55
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:14,670
year... and we buy almost all of them from abroad.

56
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,430
And more than eight out of every ten come from one country.

57
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:19,310
China.

58
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:21,220
So you're probably thinking —

59
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:22,280
if the sand is ours,

60
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,610
why can't we just dig it up and make them?

61
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:26,180
Let's open that box.

62
00:02:26,910 --> 00:02:29,670
Here's the catch, and it may surprise you.

63
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,270
Rare earths are not actually rare.

64
00:02:32,670 --> 00:02:35,050
The rare part is getting them out clean.

65
00:02:35,370 --> 00:02:36,650
There are 17 of them.

66
00:02:36,910 --> 00:02:38,080
And when you dig them up,

67
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:39,520
you get them mixed together.

68
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:44,310
Think of them as 17 brothers and sisters who look almost exactly alike.

69
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:46,940
Nearly the same size, same habits,

70
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:48,730
almost the same chemistry.

71
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:51,040
To your eye, and to most chemicals,

72
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,220
they look the same.

73
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:55,040
So how do you pull one of them out of the crowd?

74
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:57,360
There's no single magic step.

75
00:02:57,570 --> 00:02:59,260
You dissolve the mix in acid,

76
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:02,240
and the liquid flows through a long row of tanks.

77
00:03:02,590 --> 00:03:05,800
Each tank pulls them apart... only a tiny bit.

78
00:03:06,070 --> 00:03:07,270
So you repeat it.

79
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,710
Again and again.

80
00:03:09,070 --> 00:03:12,260
A big plant can run hundreds of these tanks in a row,

81
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:14,180
just to get one element clean.

82
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:16,400
Think of it like climbing stairs.

83
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:19,990
Each tank is one step... it lifts you only a little.

84
00:03:20,410 --> 00:03:22,470
Want one rare earth, nearly pure?

85
00:03:22,830 --> 00:03:24,650
You climb hundreds of steps.

86
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:26,380
And that's only the first half.

87
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:28,300
The second half is faster.

88
00:03:28,570 --> 00:03:29,600
Let me run you through it.

89
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:32,730
Next, the clean rare earth becomes a metal.

90
00:03:32,970 --> 00:03:37,320
You melt it with iron and boron... and that mix is called an alloy.

91
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:40,030
Then you cool it into thin pieces.

92
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,300
Hydrogen gas cracks those pieces,

93
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:45,410
and you grind them into a powder finer than flour.

94
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:49,040
You line that powder up inside a strong magnetic field,

95
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,350
press it into a block,

96
00:03:50,350 --> 00:03:53,340
and bake it at about 1,000 degrees Celsius.

97
00:03:53,690 --> 00:03:56,880
Only at the very end do you switch on its magnetism.

98
00:03:57,250 --> 00:03:59,670
That's when you finally have a magnet.

99
00:04:00,350 --> 00:04:02,680
So a magnet isn't one factory.

100
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:03,740
It's a chain.

101
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:06,110
Sand, to mixed rare earths,

102
00:04:06,110 --> 00:04:09,470
to clean rare earth powder, to metal, to alloy,

103
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:10,310
to magnet.

104
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,800
Miss one link... and you're stuck.

105
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:14,270
Remember this chain.

106
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:15,750
It's the whole story.

107
00:04:16,230 --> 00:04:19,140
So how did China end up leading every link?

108
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:20,890
In 1992,

109
00:04:20,890 --> 00:04:24,180
China's leader Deng Xiaoping is reported to have said

110
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,800
— the Middle East has oil,

111
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,290
China has rare earths.

112
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:30,160
And China treated it like a national mission.

113
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,350
Long-term, and patient.

114
00:04:32,610 --> 00:04:34,110
Until about 40 years ago,

115
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:36,630
America made most of the world's rare earths.

116
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:38,580
Then the work moved to China,

117
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,750
where labour was cheaper and pollution rules were weaker.

118
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:44,730
Because separating rare earths is dirty work.

119
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:46,090
Strong acids.

120
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:47,220
Lots of waste.

121
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:50,120
Most countries were happy to let someone else do it.

122
00:04:50,490 --> 00:04:53,790
So China did it for 30 years... and got very,

123
00:04:53,790 --> 00:04:54,980
very good at it.

124
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:57,660
Now look at where that leaves you and me today.

125
00:04:58,010 --> 00:04:59,970
Digging up the rare earths for magnets?

126
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:02,130
China does about six out of ten.

127
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:03,190
Cleaning them?

128
00:05:03,450 --> 00:05:04,740
More than eight out of ten.

129
00:05:05,110 --> 00:05:06,230
Making the magnets?

130
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:07,850
More than nine out of ten.

131
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:10,400
That's from the International Energy Agency.

132
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:11,880
Do you notice something?

133
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:13,930
Digging is the easy part.

134
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:18,990
The tanks and the furnaces are the hard part... and China runs most of them.

135
00:05:19,710 --> 00:05:21,180
So what about India?

136
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:23,110
We had the sand all along.

137
00:05:23,450 --> 00:05:24,330
What stopped us?

138
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:25,880
I'll give you two things.

139
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,680
What's inside our sand.

140
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:29,570
And what we did with it.

141
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:30,490
In India,

142
00:05:30,490 --> 00:05:33,870
rare earths mostly come in a mineral called monazite.

143
00:05:34,110 --> 00:05:37,870
You'll find it in the dark sand on some beaches in the south and east.

144
00:05:38,170 --> 00:05:40,590
And monazite has a surprise inside it.

145
00:05:40,890 --> 00:05:41,510
Thorium.

146
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:42,850
It's radioactive,

147
00:05:42,850 --> 00:05:45,030
and it can be used as nuclear fuel.

148
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:47,340
And that one fact, as you'll see,

149
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:49,690
changed how India handled this sand.

150
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:50,720
So by law,

151
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:53,520
monazite is treated as an atomic material.

152
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,260
Under the Atomic Energy Act,

153
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:58,230
only one government company is allowed to process it.

154
00:05:58,410 --> 00:06:00,190
Indian Rare Earths Limited —

155
00:06:00,190 --> 00:06:02,400
today it's simply called IREL

156
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:05,070
If you think about it, that kept things safe.

157
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:08,330
But for decades it also kept the business small.

158
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:13,330
Even India's own mining bureau wrote that demand for rare earths at home was limited.

159
00:06:13,690 --> 00:06:15,150
And here's the painful part.

160
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,570
In 2024,

161
00:06:16,570 --> 00:06:20,640
IREL produced about 2,900 tonnes of rare earths.

162
00:06:20,810 --> 00:06:23,200
And more than 1,000 tonnes went to Japan,

163
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:25,510
under a deal signed back in 2012.

164
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,620
Think about it.

165
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:30,570
You send the raw material out... and you buy the finished magnets in.

166
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:32,360
So you sell the cheap part,

167
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:34,300
and you buy back the costly part.

168
00:06:34,650 --> 00:06:36,330
There's one more honest problem.

169
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:39,150
Our sand is rich in the lighter rare earths,

170
00:06:39,150 --> 00:06:40,150
like neodymium.

171
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:45,320
But a magnet inside a hot motor also needs a little of two heavier ones

172
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:46,970
— dysprosium and terbium —

173
00:06:46,970 --> 00:06:49,180
to keep its strength in the heat.

174
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:53,580
Our own atomic energy department says India has very little of those.

175
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:56,130
For now, we depend on others for them.

176
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:59,110
So the sand alone was never going to be enough.

177
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:00,910
You need the whole chain.

178
00:07:01,270 --> 00:07:03,030
And then came the wake-up call.

179
00:07:03,410 --> 00:07:04,950
April, 2025.

180
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:08,820
China said companies now need special permission to send out

181
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:11,940
seven rare earths... and the magnets made with them.

182
00:07:12,350 --> 00:07:13,590
Permission takes time.

183
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:16,170
And while you wait, your supply dries up.

184
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:18,790
You saw what that did to Bajaj by July.

185
00:07:19,050 --> 00:07:21,190
Ather and TVS felt the pressure too.

186
00:07:21,510 --> 00:07:23,950
Back in April, Rajiv Bajaj had warned —

187
00:07:23,950 --> 00:07:25,900
if China stopped these magnets,

188
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:30,030
India's whole electric vehicle industry could halt within weeks.

189
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:30,690
Later,

190
00:07:30,690 --> 00:07:33,970
China started giving permission to some Indian companies.

191
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:35,280
But there was a condition.

192
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:38,030
You couldn't use those magnets for defence.

193
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:40,390
Then in October 2025,

194
00:07:40,390 --> 00:07:42,610
China announced even tougher rules.

195
00:07:42,870 --> 00:07:45,410
But after talks with America, it paused them —

196
00:07:45,410 --> 00:07:46,250
for one year.

197
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:48,530
That pause ends on November 10,

198
00:07:48,530 --> 00:07:49,690
2026.

199
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:54,150
America and China have already stretched their own trade deal till January.

200
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:55,580
So here's what you watch.

201
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:59,170
Will China stretch this pause too... or let it end?

202
00:07:59,530 --> 00:08:00,920
And the April permission rule?

203
00:08:01,210 --> 00:08:02,290
It never went away.

204
00:08:03,050 --> 00:08:05,010
So is India just waiting?

205
00:08:05,390 --> 00:08:08,280
Not at all — and this part might surprise you.

206
00:08:08,660 --> 00:08:09,720
In Visakhapatnam,

207
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:12,770
on a campus of the Bhabha Atomic Research Centre,

208
00:08:12,770 --> 00:08:15,690
India already runs a rare earth magnet plant.

209
00:08:15,990 --> 00:08:18,090
It's built with our own technology,

210
00:08:18,090 --> 00:08:20,070
from Bhabha and a DRDO lab.

211
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:23,510
And it makes a special magnet that can take high heat,

212
00:08:23,510 --> 00:08:25,710
the kind used in defence and space.

213
00:08:25,990 --> 00:08:27,570
In November 2025,

214
00:08:27,570 --> 00:08:32,130
the government approved a scheme worth about ₹7,300 crore.

215
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:32,930
The goal?

216
00:08:33,210 --> 00:08:35,840
6,000 tonnes of magnets a year,

217
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:36,930
made in India.

218
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,790
And the full chain — from rare earth powder,

219
00:08:39,790 --> 00:08:42,200
to metal, to alloy, to finished magnet.

220
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:44,160
Five companies will share that.

221
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:46,020
In August 2026,

222
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:47,320
20 bids came in.

223
00:08:47,590 --> 00:08:50,620
Among them, L&T, Coal India and ReNew.

224
00:08:50,850 --> 00:08:52,640
The winners are still to be announced,

225
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,990
so keep your eyes on this.

226
00:08:54,210 --> 00:08:58,820
The 2026 budget also announced special rare earth zones in Odisha,

227
00:08:58,820 --> 00:09:01,150
Kerala, Andhra Pradesh and Tamil Nadu.

228
00:09:01,350 --> 00:09:04,200
Mining, processing, research and factories,

229
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,250
all linked up.

230
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,140
And remember the Japan deal?

231
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:08,960
In June 2025,

232
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:12,760
Reuters reported that India asked IREL to stop those exports,

233
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,810
and keep the rare earths at home.

234
00:09:15,030 --> 00:09:17,310
So the plan is to keep the sand here.

235
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,850
The money is here.

236
00:09:19,070 --> 00:09:21,720
Now comes the hard middle you saw in that chain.

237
00:09:22,490 --> 00:09:24,780
Let me be honest with you about the timeline.

238
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:26,150
Under the scheme,

239
00:09:26,150 --> 00:09:28,060
plants get two years to be built.

240
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:30,000
Then five years of support.

241
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:33,720
And China has a head start of more than 30 years.

242
00:09:34,090 --> 00:09:36,070
Running hundreds of tanks well,

243
00:09:36,070 --> 00:09:38,300
every single day, takes practice.

244
00:09:38,670 --> 00:09:40,010
You can't buy that overnight.

245
00:09:40,410 --> 00:09:42,440
So here's the rule I take from all this.

246
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:44,470
If you only sell the sand,

247
00:09:44,470 --> 00:09:46,900
you sell cheap and you buy expensive.

248
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:48,280
And the price of that?

249
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:50,340
When the one seller says stop,

250
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:51,630
your factories stop.

251
00:09:52,150 --> 00:09:53,110
You saw it in Pune.

252
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:55,010
But here's the reality today.

253
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,740
India has the sand.

254
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:58,210
It has the scientists.

255
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:00,060
And now it has the money.

256
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:03,350
What's left is the hard middle — more tanks,

257
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:04,600
and the furnaces.

258
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:06,470
So what does this mean for you?

259
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:09,970
If you're planning to buy an electric scooter or a new phone,

260
00:10:09,970 --> 00:10:10,800
remember this.

261
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:14,000
A small magnet inside it depends on this chain

262
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,020
— and that can change its price,

263
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:18,600
and even when it reaches your showroom.

264
00:10:18,970 --> 00:10:19,940
Watch two things.

265
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,730
November 10 — does China's pause end,

266
00:10:22,730 --> 00:10:23,890
or get stretched?

267
00:10:24,170 --> 00:10:25,530
And the scheme winners —

268
00:10:25,530 --> 00:10:29,160
the five companies that will try to build India's own magnets.

269
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:31,310
India won't fix this in one jump.

270
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:34,600
It'll be tank by tank... furnace by furnace.

271
